<title>BELGIUM: EU confirms it cleared Fortis buy of MeesPierson.</title>
<headline>EU confirms it cleared Fortis buy of MeesPierson.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it has approved the acquisition of merchant bank MeesPierson NV by Belgian-Dutch insurance and banking group Fortis.</p>
<p>Fortis, which is owned by Fortis AG and Fortis Amev NV, announced last month it had sealed the takeover of MeesPierson from Dutch bank ABN AMRO for 2.5 billion guilders.</p>
<p>&quot;The new entity will compete with players of the size of ABN AMRO, ING Bank and Rabobank. Apart from these three banks, some fifty other banks are active on the Dutch market,&quot; the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;This operation will put an end to the considerable overlap of activities which exists at present between MeesPierson and ABN AMRO,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The deal was submitted for clearance on January 3 under the European Union's merger regulation which bans creation or strengthening of dominant positions.</p>
<p>-- Fredrik Dahl +32 2 287 68 11</p>
